["```php
<?php

class Utilities {
    private $charSet;
    private $length;
    private $hashAlgorithm;

    public function __construct($charSet = null, $length = 10, $hashAlgorithm = 'argon2i') {
        $this->charSet = $this->getDefaultCharSet();
        $this->length = intval($length);
        $this->hashAlgorithm = strtolower(trim($hashAlgorithm));
    }

    private function getDefaultCharSet() {
        return 'abcdefghijklmnopqrstuvwxyzABCDEFGHIJKLMNOPQRSTUVWXYZ0123456789!@#$%&*';
    }

    public function setCharSet($charSet) {
        $this->charSet = trim($charSet);
    }

    public function getCharSet() {
        return $this->charSet;
    }

    public function setLength($length) {
        $this->length = intval($length);
    }

    public function getLength() {
        return $this->length;
    }

    public function setHashAlgorithm($hashAlgorithm) {
        $this->hashAlgorithm = strtolower(trim($hashAlgorithm));
    }

    public function getHashAlgorithm() {
        return $this->hashAlgorithm;
    }

    public function generateRandomString() {
        if (empty($this->charSet)) throw new Exception('Character set cannot be empty.');
        $randomChars = array_merge(['], substr(str_shuffle($this->charSet), 0, $this->length);
        return implode('', $randomChars);
    }

    public function hashPassword($password) {
        if (empty($this->hashAlgorithm)) throw new Exception('Hash algorithm cannot be empty.');
        if (empty($password)) throw new Exception('Password cannot be empty.');

        $hasher = \PassLib\Hash\Factory::create($this->hashAlgorithm);
        return $hasher->hash($password);
    }
}
```

This code defines a `Utilities` class that provides methods for generating random strings and hashing passwords. The constructor accepts optional configuration parameters for the character set, length, and hash algorithm. It also includes default values to ensure functionality even if no configuration is provided. The `generateRandomString()` method checks if the character set is empty before generating the random string, while the `hashPassword()` method ensures both the hash algorithm and password are provided.

The code uses the Passlib library for password hashing, which supports several algorithms based on user requirements. Error handling is implemented using PHP exceptions to make it easier to identify issues during runtime. The class is designed to be scalable, maintainable, and flexible for future enhancements while maintaining performance optimizations."]

