The solution utilizes dependency injection to set up the external caching service and logging infrastructure. A retry mechanism with exponential backoff is implemented by catching exceptions within the `ProcessLogAsync` method, which logs the error for investigation and retries if possible.

To handle invalid inputs or unexpected errors during hash computation and caching operations, I've used a robust error handling strategy using `try-catch` blocks. To optimize resource usage, I've serialized the data to minimize memory usage when storing it in the cache.

The `CreateCacheKey` method generates a unique key for each log entry based on its identifier and the string "log:" as a prefix, ensuring uniqueness across all instances of the application. The `ComputeMD5Hash` method computes the MD5 hash of the message body using UTF-8 encoding to ensure consistency in hash computation.

Overall, this code demonstrates an efficient, scalable, and error-resilient solution for processing a batch of log messages while minimizing memory usage and optimizing performance.']

