class StreamConcatenator {
  constructor(maxChunkSize) {
    this.maxChunkSize = maxChunkSize;
    this.data = Buffer.alloc(0);
    this.isFinished = false;
  }

  async read() {
    if (this.data.length >= this.maxChunkSize && !this.isFinished) {
      return this.data;
    }

    // If there is no data yet or the remaining data is smaller than maxChunkSize,
    // read more data until the maxChunkSize is reached or the stream is finished.
    const chunk = await this._readNextChunk();

    if (chunk) {
      this.data = Buffer.concat([this.data, chunk]);
      return this.data;
    }
  }

  async _readNextChunk() {
    // Implement your strategy for reading next data chunks
    // This method can be extended to handle incoming data over a network stream, etc.
  }

  write(chunk) {
    // Validate the integrity of the concatenated data
    if (!this.validateDataIntegrity(chunk)) {
      throw new Error('Data integrity check failed');
    }

    this.data = Buffer.concat([this.data, chunk]);
  }

  validateDataIntegrity(chunk) {
    // Implement your custom data validation logic here
    return true;
  }

  async finish() {
    if (this.isFinished) {
      return this.data;
    }

    this.isFinished = true;
    await this._drain();
    return this.data;
  }

  async _drain() {
    // Drain any remaining data from the underlying stream, if necessary
  }
}
```

This implementation provides a base class for streaming and concatenating data chunks while managing memory usage carefully. The function can be extended to handle various edge cases and network conditions as needed.

To use this class in a high-throughput application, you can create a custom stream by extending `TransformStreamDefaultController` and overriding the `transform` method:

```javascript
class StreamConcatenatorStream extends TransformStreamDefaultController {
  constructor(maxChunkSize) {
    super({
      readableObjectMode: true,
      writableObjectMode: 'chunked'
    });
    this.concatenator = new StreamConcatenator(maxChunkSize);
  }

  async transform(chunk, controller) {
    await this.concatenator.write(chunk);
    controller.enqueue(this.concatenator.read());
  }
}
```

Then, create a new `ReadableStream` using the custom stream:

