    - MAC address: 6 bytes (12 digits, e.g., "00:1A:3B:4C:5D:6E")
    - IP address: Variable-length string (e.g., "192.168.1.1")
    - Link state: 1 byte (Boolean value as 0 for false and 1 for true)

This approach allows for easy extension of the NICP configuration struct by adding new fields at the end, without affecting the existing format. The deserialization process can simply skip any added fields it does not recognize.']

