The function includes error checking for each memory allocation and handles allocation failures gracefully by cleaning up any partially allocated resources before returning an appropriate error status. The function also provides a clean interface for incrementing and decrementing reference counts, and correctly handles the deallocation of resources when the reference count reaches zero.

The code is thread-safe and does not rely on global variables. Instead, it uses static variables within the function to maintain state between function calls if necessary. The memory pool can be initialized with a specified capacity, allowing for efficient memory management even when the number of `data_points` is very large.']

